Frankly, I'm not sure. Given how the game usually works my speculation
is that the enchantment will just be added to the damage delt, and if
you are two-weaponing probably even twice. Early on such a damage bonus
may be very helpful (though my experience suggests that you won't get
a significant enchantment without explicitly charging it). For Astral,
if I am playing melee fighters or have no good ranged attacks at hand,
I want to deal as many damage as possible, specifically for the Riders
(with speed and unburdened you can deal two melee hits, and that is
IME sufficient to kill them with good melee weapons and damage boni,
and also mind that wands of death often miss, and they fail for Death)
but at that place it's also generally useful. So I think your question
(a) is answered by; deal extra damage to kill monsters quicker if you
have a spare ring finger available. And I second your answer to your
question (b). Scrolls of charging are rare and usually better spent
for other purposes.

In my game I blew up one +3 ring and left the second at +4, fearing
it will get destroyed as well. I had another (third) ring so I could
have experimented to increase the limit, but I was unaware how fast
I can invoke the PYEC again without getting my request ignored.[*]

